Falsifies `block_roster_contract::capacity_of_fits_the_page_for_every_length`.

The defect: `capacity_of` divides the whole page length by `ENTRY_BYTES` and
forgets the header, the slip a writer makes when it thinks of the page as all
entries. Every page then claims two entries more than it has room for, so a
writer that trusts the figure lays its last entries past the page's end.

Expected to fail: `assert!(HEADER_BYTES + capacity * ENTRY_BYTES <= len)`, on
any length that holds the header.


diff --git a/src/lib.rs b/src/lib.rs
--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -134,7 +134,7 @@
     if len < HEADER_BYTES {
         0
     } else {
-        (len - HEADER_BYTES) / ENTRY_BYTES
+        len / ENTRY_BYTES
     }
 }
 
